# Human Flourishing License

## Version 1.0

Copyright © [2026] [Chinese For Everyone].

### Preamble

This License exists to preserve four principles:

**Everyone must be able to use the Software on equal terms.
No person may receive less functionality because they have less money.
The Software must remain open and continuable.
The Software must be used for genuine human benefit, not for human harm.**

These principles are the foundation of the License and shall guide its interpretation.

### 1. Definitions

**“Software”** means the software and source materials released by the Copyright Holder under this License.

**“Covered Work”** means the Software and any work that incorporates, modifies, extends, or is substantially derived from it.

**“Functionality”** means the capabilities materially provided by a Covered Work.

**“User”** means any natural person who uses a Covered Work.

**“Commercial Use”** means use intended to obtain revenue, monetary compensation, or commercial advantage, whether directly or indirectly.

**“Economic Condition”** means payment, subscription, purchase, donation, paid account, credit, licence fee, sponsorship, or any other transfer of money or economic value required or used to obtain, retain, improve, accelerate, increase, or unlock access to Functionality.

**“Donation”** means a voluntary transfer of value for which the donor receives no consideration.

**“Consideration”** means anything of economic, functional, preferential, or practical value provided in exchange for a Donation or other payment.

**“Reliable Evidence”** means independently verifiable empirical research, systematic reviews or meta-analyses, controlled studies where reasonably applicable, or conclusions supported by established professional or scientific bodies relevant to the claimed benefit.

### 2. Grant of Rights

Subject to this License, every person receives a worldwide, perpetual, royalty-free right to access, use, copy, modify, run, and distribute the Software and Covered Works.

These rights exist only while the conditions of this License are observed.

### 3. Non-Commercial Use

Commercial Use of the Software or any Covered Work is prohibited.

The Software and Covered Works must not be sold, rented, licensed, monetized, commercially hosted, commercially provided, or used primarily to obtain commercial advantage.

### 4. Equal Access

Every User must receive the same Functionality under the same substantive conditions, regardless of wealth, income, ability to pay, payment status, or economic circumstances.

No Covered Work may impose an Economic Condition for access to any Functionality.

No Covered Work may provide a materially better, larger, faster, more capable, less restricted, or otherwise superior form of Functionality to one User because that User has paid or provided economic value.

No Covered Work may divide its Functionality into free and paid versions or otherwise reserve Functionality for paying Users.

A limitation is permitted only when it applies equally to all Users and cannot be removed, increased, or reduced through payment or economic status.

This requirement applies equally to Functionality provided through third-party software, services, APIs, models, infrastructure, or other dependencies. A User must not be required to pay a third party in order to receive Functionality.

### 5. Donations

Donations are permitted only when they are entirely voluntary and provide no Consideration.

A donor must receive no additional Functionality, access, capacity, priority, quality, service, status, preference, or other advantage.

A payment that provides any such advantage is not a Donation and is prohibited.

### 6. Source and Same License

The complete source code necessary to inspect, modify, build, operate, and reproduce the Functionality of a Covered Work must be available without charge under this License.

For a Covered Work operated over a network, the source necessary to reproduce the network service and its Functionality must likewise be made available under this License to its Users.

Every Covered Work must be distributed under this License and no other license.

No person may relicense, sublicense, or impose terms on a Covered Work that permit conduct prohibited by this License.

Independent third-party components remain subject to their own licenses where their copyright holders require it.

### 7. Human Benefit

A Covered Work may be distributed or operated only if its primary intended purpose is to provide meaningful benefit to human beings.

For this purpose, a benefit must concern a real improvement in human welfare or capability, supported where applicable by Reliable Evidence. Examples include education and learning, intellectual development, physical health, mental well-being, meaningful social connection, cultural participation or creation, practical capability, autonomy, or other demonstrable aspects of human flourishing.

Entertainment or emotional enjoyment alone is not sufficient where the primary mechanism of the Covered Work is to produce compulsive use or dependency.

A Covered Work violates this Section when its primary purpose or reasonably foreseeable principal mechanism is to create or maintain compulsive use, dependency, or other material impairment of a person's ability to stop using it or to pursue ordinary activities beneficial to their life.

The burden of establishing that a Covered Work satisfies this Section lies with the Licensee. The assessment must be based on the weight of Reliable Evidence rather than on the Licensee's personal belief, commercial interest, or assertion.

Where Reliable Evidence establishes a substantial and reasonably foreseeable risk of material harm that is not outweighed by the human benefit of the relevant Functionality, that Functionality must not be distributed under this License.

### 8. Prohibited Use

A Covered Work must not be used primarily to produce or distribute material that:

(a) discriminates against or promotes the unequal treatment or subordination of persons on the basis of race, sex, sexual orientation, religion, nationality, disability, or age;

(b) is pornographic, obscene, or sexually explicit.

### 9. No Circumvention

No person may avoid a requirement of this License by moving a prohibited payment condition, restriction, superior Functionality, source code, or other mechanism into another component, server, service, account system, plugin, extension, dependency, or other separate work.

A Covered Work must not be divided or reorganized for the purpose of achieving a result that this License prohibits when considered as a whole.

### 10. Violation and Termination

A material violation of this License automatically terminates the rights granted to the violating Licensee.

A violation by an end User does not by itself terminate the rights of an operator who did not participate in, intentionally enable, or knowingly permit the violation and who takes reasonable steps to stop it after becoming aware of it.

Termination removes the rights granted by this License; it does not transfer ownership of copyright or other property.

### 11. Notices

Every copy and Covered Work must retain the copyright notice and the complete text of this License.

### 12. Disclaimer

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED “AS IS”, WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW.

### 13. Severability

If any provision of this License is held unenforceable, the remaining provisions remain in effect to the maximum extent permitted by law.

### 14. Governing Principle

This License shall, to the maximum extent permitted by law, be interpreted to preserve its essential purposes:


**The Software is for everyone.
No one's access depends on wealth.
Its capabilities cannot be sold, restricted, or reserved for those who can pay.
Its source must remain available and its continuation must remain possible.
And the Software must provide genuine human benefit rather than being designed to exploit, degrade, or materially harm the people who use it.**
